![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Replace the locale-sensitive `Intl.Collator` comparison with a strict lexicographical byte-order comparison. This ensures absolute determinism across all environments and aligns with the repository's sorting guidelines.

```javascript
function compareNatural(left, right) {
  if (left === null || left === undefined) return right === null || right === undefined ? 0 : -1;
  if (right === null || right === undefined) return 1;
  const s1 = String(left);
  const s2 = String(right);
  return s1 < s2 ? -1 : s1 > s2 ? 1 : 0;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When sorting JSON arrays lexicographically by an ID field to prevent diff churn, verify the sorting using a strict byte-order comparison (such as Buffer.compare).
</details>

